#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Build and test each open pull request's head on this host; post the verdict.

The default branch's protection requires a commit status
(`checks.context`, say `vm/build-and-test`), and this is what produces
it: the checks every agent runs before pushing, run again on the pull
request's head on this host rather than on GitHub Actions. The Merger
merges on that status (`forge-merger`).

    forge-pr-check                       from cron: start a check of the
                                         oldest waiting head, if none runs
    forge-pr-check --post                the same, posting each verdict
    forge-pr-check --worker SHA --pr N   the check itself (started by the
                                         above; also runnable by hand)

**The cron tick returns at once and the check runs detached.**
`forge-cron-run` holds locks while a job runs, so a long test run under
it would starve the rest of the schedule. The worker is started with
its own session and no inherited descriptors, so it doesn't keep them
either.

**`checks.slots` checks at a time** (default 2; `$FORGE_PR_CHECK_SLOTS`
overrides it). A worker holds its slot's lock in the state directory
while it runs, `worker.lock` for slot 1 and `worker-N.lock` for slot N;
its one line names the pull request, head and start. Each slot has its
own worktree (`wt`, `wt-N`) and its own build caches (`checks.caches`,
below), so two checks never share a checkout or wait on each other's
cache lock. A tick starts the oldest waiting head that no slot is
running, in the first free slot, and starts nothing when every slot is
held. The kernel drops a lock however its holder dies, so a killed
worker is never reported as running.

**Oldest-waiting first.** A head waits from when a tick first sees it.
Drafts are not checked. A head whose worktree can't be prepared goes
behind every other, and after MAX_ERRORS failures it is given up on,
so one unfetchable ref can't hold the queue. A head that moved before
its check started is dropped; the new head is queued in its place.

**A head just started isn't started again.** Until its worker has
taken its slot's lock and said who it is, nothing else shows the head
is being checked, and a tick in that window (from cron, an event, or a
worker's chained tick) would start it again in another slot: a
duplicate run and a duplicate post. So the tick that starts a head
stamps `started` on its waiting entry, under the state lock, and
`next_head` skips a head started less than START_GRACE ago. A worker
that dies before taking its lock leaves its head pickable again once
the grace is up.

**With `checks.merger_first` on, the Merger's pull request goes first**
(default off). The Merger writes `next.json` in its state directory
each tick, naming the pull request it is waiting on (`--merger-dir`,
default ~/.local/state/agent-forge/<project>/merger). That head is
checked before every other, since the next merge waits on its verdict.
**While the Merger names a pull request, nothing else is started**,
even in a free slot, and even when that pull request's head isn't
waiting yet (the Merger is about to update it, or it was checked and
the Merger waits on something else). Under strict branch protection
any other head's verdict is spent once the next merge moves the
default branch, and a check started now would hold a slot for minutes
just as the Merger's pull request needs one. The tick says `HELD`. Its
head given up on after MAX_ERRORS failures doesn't hold anything, and
nor does a `next.json` older than MERGER_FRESH, which a Merger that has
stopped leaves behind: a stopped Merger must not hold every check. So
the Merger has to tick more often than that for the rule to hold.
Without branch protection that requires heads to be up to date, a
verdict outlives the next merge and holding the slots only delays it,
which is why the rule is off unless the project turns it on.

**A head from another repository is refused.** The steps run the pull
request's own code with this user's access to the host, so only
branches of this repository are run.

**The steps are the configuration's**, `checks.steps`: each
`{"name": ..., "run": [argv], "only_if": path}`, `only_if` naming a
file the head must have for the step to run (default: one step, `make
test`). The list comes from the cron checkout, so a pull request can't
change which checks it is judged by; what each target does is the
head's own. Each step runs even if an earlier one failed, and none is
retried. They run in a clean, detached worktree of the head (`wt` in
the state directory), without `GH_TOKEN` or any `FORGE_` setting, so a
test can't behave differently here for having one. `checks.caches`
maps an environment variable to a directory name, such as
`{"CARGO_TARGET_DIR": "cargo-target"}`: each slot gets its own such
directory in the state directory, outside the worktree, so a head isn't
built from nothing each time. A variable the host already sets wins.
A step is stopped after `checks.step_timeout_minutes` (default 30).

**Each step runs under a memory limit**, in its own `systemd-run
--user --scope` with `MemoryMax` (`checks.memory_max`, default `16G`;
`$FORGE_PR_CHECK_MEMORY_MAX` overrides it; `off` for none) and no swap.
Its `OOMPolicy` is `continue`, so a test that runs out is killed alone:
the step fails with that test's output, rather than systemd stopping
the whole step without a word. A worker that can't start a user scope
says so in `worker.log` and runs its steps without the limit.

**Without `--post` it posts nothing.** It reads the open pull requests
as the poster's App either way (`checks.poster`, default the Merger),
minting its token with `forge-app-token`.

**`--post` writes the status** as that App, which needs *Commit
statuses: write*: `pending` when the steps start, then `success`, or
`failure` naming the first failed step. A head refused or given up on
gets `error`, saying why, since the Merger would otherwise wait on it
for a status that never comes. The Merger counts only statuses that App
posted. A post GitHub refuses changes neither the verdict nor the exit
status: each tick posts again any verdict on a still-open head that
never reached GitHub. A worker killed mid-run leaves `pending`, and its
head still waiting, so the next check replaces it.

**A posting worker starts the next tick when it lets the lock go**,
through `forge-cron-run`, so a head that arrived while it ran waits for
that rather than for the next cron minute. A tick with nothing to do
starts nothing, which ends the chain. A head that could not be checked
out is still waiting, so it is left for cron's next tick rather than
retried at once.

The state directory (`--state-dir`, default
~/.local/state/agent-forge/<project>/pr-check) holds `state.json` (the
queue, and each verdict for KEEP), `verdicts.log` (one line per
verdict, refusal and give-up), and `worker.log`, each worker's output:
every step's exit status and time, and under a failed step its last
TAIL_LINES lines, each prefixed `    | `. The status names the failed
step and nothing more; why it failed is in `worker.log`.

The checkout is the cron checkout (`--checkout`, default
`$FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT`), kept at the default branch.

Exit 0 when the tick ran or the check was green, 1 from a red check,
and 2 when the question could not be asked.
"""

import argparse
import datetime
import json
import os
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time

sys.path.insert(0, os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))))
from agent_forge import config, locks  # noqa: E402

BIN = os.path.dirname(os.path.realpath(__file__))

# Set from the project's configuration by `configure`; these are the
# defaults it starts from.
REPO_SLUG = ""
MAIN = "main"
# The configuration file, for forge-app-token, whatever the cwd.
CONFIG_PATH = None
# The commit status this posts, and the App it posts and reads as.
DEFAULT_CONTEXT = "vm/build-and-test"
STATUS_CONTEXT = DEFAULT_CONTEXT
POSTER = "Merger"
HOST = ""
# What the worker runs, in order: (name, argv, run only if this path
# exists in the head, or None).
DEFAULT_STEPS = [("test", ["make", "test"], None)]
STEPS = DEFAULT_STEPS
# {environment variable: directory name} for each slot's build caches.
CACHES = {}
DEFAULT_STEP_TIMEOUT_S = 30 * 60
STEP_TIMEOUT_S = DEFAULT_STEP_TIMEOUT_S
# Each step's memory limit, in systemd's syntax; FORGE_PR_CHECK_MEMORY_MAX
# overrides it, and "off" runs the steps without one.
DEFAULT_MEMORY_MAX = "16G"
MEMORY_MAX = DEFAULT_MEMORY_MAX
# Lines of a failed step's output kept in worker.log.
TAIL_LINES = 40
# Verdicts older than this are dropped from state.json.
KEEP = datetime.timedelta(days=21)
# Failures to prepare a head's worktree before it is given up on.
MAX_ERRORS = 3
# How long a head just started is left to its worker before another
# tick may start it: longer than a worker takes to take its lock.
START_GRACE = datetime.timedelta(seconds=60)
# Checks run at once; FORGE_PR_CHECK_SLOTS overrides it.
DEFAULT_SLOTS = 2
SLOTS = DEFAULT_SLOTS
# GitHub refuses a status description longer than this.
DESCRIPTION_MAX = 140
# The most unposted verdicts one tick posts again, oldest first.
POST_BATCH = 10
# Never passed to the steps: they must not act on GitHub, and a test in
# the head must not find this tool's state or settings. Nor is any
# variable starting STEP_DROP_PREFIX.
STEP_DROP_ENV = ("GH_TOKEN", "GITHUB_TOKEN")
STEP_DROP_PREFIX = "FORGE_"
CRON_RUN = os.path.join(BIN, "forge-cron-run")
# What a posting worker starts when it is done: its own cron line.
NEXT_TICK = ("forge-pr-check", "--post")
# Whether the head of the pull request the Merger waits on goes first,
# holding every other check while it names one.
DEFAULT_MERGER_FIRST = False
MERGER_FIRST = DEFAULT_MERGER_FIRST
# How old the Merger's next.json may be and still be obeyed. An older
# one means the Merger has stopped, and a stopped Merger must not hold
# a pull request's place at the front, or every other check behind it.
MERGER_FRESH = datetime.timedelta(minutes=10)


def configure(project):
    """Set the module's settings from `project`, a loaded configuration:
    its repository and default branch, and the `checks` section
    (`context`, `poster`, `steps`, `caches`, `slots`, `memory_max`,
    `step_timeout_minutes`, `merger_first`), each with the default
    above."""
    global REPO_SLUG, MAIN, CONFIG_PATH, STATUS_CONTEXT, POSTER, HOST
    global STEPS, CACHES, SLOTS, MEMORY_MAX, STEP_TIMEOUT_S, MERGER_FIRST
    checks = project.section("checks")
    REPO_SLUG, MAIN = project.repo, project.default_branch
    CONFIG_PATH = project.path
    STATUS_CONTEXT = checks.get("context", DEFAULT_CONTEXT)
    POSTER = checks.get("poster",
                        project.section("merge").get("merger", "Merger"))
    HOST = project.host
    STEPS = [(s["name"], list(s["run"]), s.get("only_if"))
             for s in checks["steps"]] if "steps" in checks else DEFAULT_STEPS
    CACHES = dict(checks.get("caches", {}))
    SLOTS = checks.get("slots", DEFAULT_SLOTS)
    MEMORY_MAX = checks.get("memory_max", DEFAULT_MEMORY_MAX)
    STEP_TIMEOUT_S = 60 * checks.get("step_timeout_minutes",
                                     DEFAULT_STEP_TIMEOUT_S // 60)
    MERGER_FIRST = checks.get("merger_first", DEFAULT_MERGER_FIRST)


def sh(args, cwd=None, env=None, timeout=None):
    """Run args; a timeout comes back as exit 124, like timeout(1)."""
    try:
        return subprocess.run(args, cwd=cwd, env=env, capture_output=True,
                              text=True, timeout=timeout)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired as err:
        out = err.stdout if isinstance(err.stdout, str) else ""
        return subprocess.CompletedProcess(
            args, 124, out, "timed out after %ss" % timeout)


def now_utc():
    return datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).replace(microsecond=0)


def iso(when):
    return when.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


def parse(stamp):
    return datetime.datetime.strptime(stamp, "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ").replace(
        tzinfo=datetime.timezone.utc)


def state_lock(state_dir):
    """Held around every read-modify-write of state.json, which the tick
    and the worker both write."""
    return locks.locked(os.path.join(state_dir, "state.lock"))


def load(state_dir):
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(state_dir, "state.json")) as handle:
            state = json.load(handle)
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        state = {}
    for key in ("waiting", "results", "refused"):
        state.setdefault(key, {})
    return state


def save(state_dir, state):
    """Written whole and renamed into place, so a reader never sees half."""
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=state_dir, prefix=".state.")
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as handle:
        json.dump(state, handle, indent=1, sort_keys=True)
    os.replace(tmp, os.path.join(state_dir, "state.json"))


def log(state_dir, line, when, out=print):
    """One line to verdicts.log, and to out."""
    text = "%s %s" % (iso(when), line)
    with open(os.path.join(state_dir, "verdicts.log"), "a") as handle:
        handle.write(text + "\n")
    out(text)


try_lock = locks.try_lock


def slot_name(name, slot):
    """`name` for slot 1, which keeps the one-slot names, else name-N."""
    return name if slot == 1 else "%s-%d" % (name, slot)


def lock_path(state_dir, slot=1):
    return os.path.join(state_dir, slot_name("worker", slot) + ".lock")


def slots_from_env(environ=None):
    """FORGE_PR_CHECK_SLOTS as an int of at least 1, else SLOTS."""
    value = (os.environ if environ is None else environ).get(
        "FORGE_PR_CHECK_SLOTS", "")
    return int(value) if value.isascii() and value.isdigit() \
        and int(value) >= 1 else SLOTS


def running(state_dir, slot=1):
    """The slot's lock holder line while someone holds it ("" if it
    hasn't said who), or None when it is free."""
    return locks.holder(lock_path(state_dir, slot))


def mint(run=sh):
    """POSTER's installation token, or None."""
    env = dict(os.environ)
    if CONFIG_PATH:
        env["FORGE_CONFIG"] = CONFIG_PATH
    got = run([os.path.join(BIN, "forge-app-token"), "--token", POSTER],
              env=env)
    token = (got.stdout or "").strip()
    return token if got.returncode == 0 and token else None


def gh(args, token, run=sh):
    return run(["gh", "api"] + args, env=dict(os.environ, GH_TOKEN=token))


def open_heads(token, run=sh):
    """[(pr, sha, head repository, draft)] for every open pull request,
    or None if GitHub could not be read. A head whose repository is gone
    reports "" for it."""
    got = gh(["--paginate", "repos/%s/pulls?state=open&per_page=100"
              % REPO_SLUG, "--jq", '.[] | [.number, .head.sha, '
              '(.head.repo.full_name // ""), .draft] | @tsv'], token, run)
    if got.returncode != 0:
        return None
    heads = []
    for line in got.stdout.splitlines():
        fields = line.split("\t")
        if len(fields) != 4 or not fields[0].isdigit() or len(fields[1]) != 40:
            return None
        heads.append((int(fields[0]), fields[1], fields[2],
                      fields[3] == "true"))
    return heads


def note_heads(state, heads, when, state_dir, out=print, post=None):
    """Queue each open, non-draft head not yet checked, refuse a foreign
    one (posting why, once, with post), and forget a waiting head that
    is no longer any pull request's."""
    current = set()
    for pr, sha, repo, draft in heads:
        if draft or sha in state["results"]:
            continue
        if repo != REPO_SLUG:
            if sha not in state["refused"]:
                state["refused"][sha] = {"pr": pr, "repo": repo,
                                         "since": iso(when)}
                where = repo or "a deleted repository"
                log(state_dir, "REFUSED #%d %s: head is in %s, not %s"
                    % (pr, sha[:10], where, REPO_SLUG), when, out)
                if post is not None:
                    post(sha, "error", "not run: the head is in %s, and "
                         "only %s's own branches are run" % (where,
                                                             REPO_SLUG))
            continue
        current.add(sha)
        state["waiting"].setdefault(sha, {"pr": pr, "since": iso(when)})
        state["waiting"][sha]["pr"] = pr
    for sha in list(state["waiting"]):
        if sha not in current:
            del state["waiting"][sha]


def just_started(entry, when):
    """Whether a waiting entry was started less than START_GRACE before
    `when`. An unreadable stamp counts as not started."""
    try:
        return when is not None and when - parse(entry["started"]) < START_GRACE
    except (KeyError, TypeError, ValueError):
        return False


def next_head(state, busy=(), first_pr=None, when=None):
    """(sha, pr) of the head that has waited longest, or None. A head
    that failed to prepare goes behind every head that has not, one
    that failed MAX_ERRORS times is not picked at all, and nor is one a
    slot is running (`busy`) or one a tick started less than
    START_GRACE before `when`.

    `first_pr` is the pull request the Merger is waiting on, or None.
    Its head goes before every other, and while it is named nothing
    else is picked: not while its head isn't waiting yet, and not while
    a slot is running it or has just been started on it (see the module
    docstring). Only once every head of it has been given up on does
    the queue go on without it."""
    waiting = state["waiting"]

    def order(sha):
        return waiting[sha].get("errors", 0), waiting[sha]["since"], sha
    if first_pr is not None:
        mine = [s for s, w in waiting.items() if w["pr"] == first_pr]
        if not mine:
            return None
        live = [s for s in mine if waiting[s].get("errors", 0) < MAX_ERRORS]
        if live:
            free = [s for s in live if s not in busy
                    and not just_started(waiting[s], when)]
            return (min(free, key=order), first_pr) if free else None
    live = [s for s, w in waiting.items()
            if w.get("errors", 0) < MAX_ERRORS and s not in busy
            and not just_started(w, when)]
    if not live:
        return None
    sha = min(live, key=order)
    return sha, waiting[sha]["pr"]


def merger_first(merger_dir, when):
    """The pull request the Merger last said it waits on, from its
    next.json, or None when there is none, it can't be read, or it is
    older than MERGER_FRESH."""
    if not merger_dir:
        return None
    try:
        with open(os.path.join(merger_dir, "next.json")) as handle:
            said = json.load(handle)
        if when - parse(said["at"]) > MERGER_FRESH:
            return None
        pr = said["pr"]
        # bool is an int to Python, never a pull request number.
        return pr if isinstance(pr, int) and not isinstance(pr, bool) \
            else None
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
        return None


def prune(state, when):
    for key, stamp in (("results", "finished"), ("refused", "since")):
        for sha in list(state[key]):
            if when - parse(state[key][sha][stamp]) > KEEP:
                del state[key][sha]


def make_poster(run=sh, out=print):
    """A post(sha, state, description) that writes STATUS_CONTEXT on sha
    as POSTER's App and returns whether GitHub took it. The token is
    minted for each post: one minted before a long check could expire."""
    def post(sha, state, description):
        token = mint(run)
        if token is None:
            out("POST-FAILED %s %s: could not mint %s's token"
                % (sha[:10], state, POSTER))
            return False
        got = gh(["-X", "POST", "repos/%s/statuses/%s" % (REPO_SLUG, sha),
                  "-f", "state=" + state, "-f", "context=" + STATUS_CONTEXT,
                  "-f", "description=" + description[:DESCRIPTION_MAX]],
                 token, run)
        if got.returncode != 0:
            out("POST-FAILED %s %s: %s" % (sha[:10], state,
                                           got.stderr.strip()))
            return False
        return True
    return post


def on_host():
    return " on " + HOST if HOST else ""


def final_status(r):
    """(state, description) for a verdict, naming the first failed step:
    where its author starts reading."""
    if r["ok"]:
        return "success", "green%s in %ds" % (on_host(), r["seconds"])
    failed = r["failed"]
    rest = " (then %s)" % ", ".join(failed[1:]) if failed[1:] else ""
    return "failure", "red%s: %s failed%s" % (on_host(), failed[0], rest)


def verdict_word(r):
    return "green" if r["ok"] else "red(%s)" % ",".join(r["failed"])


def repost(state, heads, post, out=print):
    """Post again, oldest first, up to POST_BATCH verdicts on open heads
    whose status never reached GitHub."""
    open_shas = {sha for _, sha, _, _ in heads}
    todo = sorted((r["finished"], sha) for sha, r in state["results"].items()
                  if sha in open_shas and r.get("posted") is not True)
    for _, sha in todo[:POST_BATCH]:
        r = state["results"][sha]
        r["posted"] = post(sha, *final_status(r))
        if r["posted"]:
            out("POSTED #%d %s: %s" % (r["pr"], sha[:10], verdict_word(r)))


def spawn_worker(state_dir, sha, pr, posting=False, slot=1, checkout=None):
    """Start the check detached; see the module docstring on the cron
    lock. Its output goes to worker.log."""
    wlog = open(os.path.join(state_dir, "worker.log"), "a")
    wlog.write("=== %s worker #%d %s slot %d ===\n"
               % (iso(now_utc()), pr, sha, slot))
    wlog.flush()
    subprocess.Popen(
        [sys.executable, os.path.abspath(__file__), "--worker", sha,
         "--pr", str(pr), "--state-dir", state_dir, "--slot", str(slot)]
        + (["--checkout", checkout] if checkout else [])
        + (["--post"] if posting else []),
        cwd=state_dir, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=wlog,
        stderr=subprocess.STDOUT, start_new_session=True, close_fds=True)
    wlog.close()


def tick(state_dir, token, run=sh, spawn=spawn_worker, out=print, when=None,
         post=None, slots=None, checkout=None, merger_dir=None):
    """Queue the open heads and start the next one in a free slot. With
    `merger_dir` (only when MERGER_FIRST), the Merger's pull request
    goes first and holds the rest."""
    when = when or now_utc()
    heads = open_heads(token, run)
    if heads is None:
        out("NO-PULLS: could not list %s's open pull requests" % REPO_SLUG)
        return 2
    with state_lock(state_dir):
        state = load(state_dir)
        note_heads(state, heads, when, state_dir, out, post)
        if post is not None:
            repost(state, heads, post, out)
        prune(state, when)
        save(state_dir, state)
        queued = set(state["waiting"])
    slots = slots or slots_from_env()
    holders = {slot: running(state_dir, slot) for slot in range(1, slots + 1)}
    busy = {h.split()[1] for h in holders.values()
            if h and len(h.split()) == 3 and h.startswith("#")}
    for slot, holder in holders.items():
        if holder is None:
            continue
        parts = holder.split()
        if len(parts) == 3 and parts[0].startswith("#"):
            out("RUNNING %s %s since %s; %d waiting"
                % (parts[0], parts[1][:10], parts[2], len(queued - busy)))
        else:
            out("BUSY: %s is held; %d waiting"
                % ("the worker lock" if slot == 1
                   else os.path.basename(lock_path(state_dir, slot)),
                   len(queued - busy)))
    free = [slot for slot, holder in holders.items() if holder is None]
    if not free:
        return 0
    held_for = merger_first(merger_dir, when)
    with state_lock(state_dir):
        state = load(state_dir)
        pick = next_head(state, busy, held_for, when)
        if pick is not None:
            state["waiting"][pick[0]]["started"] = iso(when)
            save(state_dir, state)
        starting = sum(1 for s, w in state["waiting"].items()
                       if s not in busy and just_started(w, when))
    if pick is None and held_for is not None and queued - busy:
        out("HELD: free slots are kept for the Merger's #%d; %d waiting"
            % (held_for, len(queued - busy)))
        return 0
    if pick is None:
        if starting:
            out("STARTING: %d just started, not yet running; %d waiting"
                % (starting, len(queued - busy) - starting))
        elif len(free) == slots:
            out("IDLE: no open head is waiting" if not queued else
                "IDLE: %d waiting, each given up on after %d failures"
                % (len(queued), MAX_ERRORS))
        return 0
    sha, pr = pick
    if checkout:
        spawn(state_dir, sha, pr, post is not None, free[0], checkout)
    else:
        spawn(state_dir, sha, pr, post is not None, free[0])
    out("STARTED #%d %s%s; %d waiting"
        % (pr, sha[:10], "" if free[0] == 1 else " in slot %d" % free[0],
           len(queued - busy) - 1))
    return 0


def prepare(repo, wt, sha, pr, run=sh):
    """Check pull request pr's head out, clean and detached, at wt,
    creating that worktree of repo the first time. Returns (status,
    detail): "ready", "moved" with the head it found instead, or
    "error"."""
    if not os.path.exists(os.path.join(wt, ".git")):
        for args in (["git", "-C", repo, "worktree", "prune"],
                     ["git", "-C", repo, "worktree", "add", "-q", "--detach",
                      "--force", wt, "origin/" + MAIN]):
            got = run(args)
            if got.returncode != 0:
                return "error", "%s: %s" % (" ".join(args[3:5]),
                                            got.stderr.strip())
    got = run(["git", "-C", wt, "fetch", "-q", "origin",
               "+refs/pull/%d/head" % pr])
    if got.returncode != 0:
        return "error", "fetch pull/%d/head: %s" % (pr, got.stderr.strip())
    got = run(["git", "-C", wt, "rev-parse", "FETCH_HEAD"])
    fetched = got.stdout.strip()
    if got.returncode != 0 or len(fetched) != 40:
        return "error", "rev-parse FETCH_HEAD: %s" % got.stderr.strip()
    if fetched != sha:
        return "moved", fetched
    for args in (["git", "-C", wt, "checkout", "-q", "--detach", "--force",
                  sha],
                 ["git", "-C", wt, "clean", "-q", "-ffdx"]):
        got = run(args)
        if got.returncode != 0:
            return "error", "%s: %s" % (" ".join(args[3:5]),
                                        got.stderr.strip())
    return "ready", ""


def step_env(state_dir, base=None, slot=1):
    """The steps' environment: `base` (os.environ) less STEP_DROP_ENV
    and every FORGE_ setting, with the slot's build caches (CACHES)
    outside the worktree unless the host set them."""
    env = {k: v for k, v in (os.environ if base is None else base).items()
           if k not in STEP_DROP_ENV and not k.startswith(STEP_DROP_PREFIX)}
    for name, folder in CACHES.items():
        env.setdefault(name, os.path.join(state_dir, slot_name(folder, slot)))
    # systemd-run --user finds the user's manager through it, and cron
    # doesn't set it.
    env.setdefault("XDG_RUNTIME_DIR", "/run/user/%d" % os.getuid())
    return env


def memory_max_from_env(environ=None):
    """The steps' memory limit, or None for none."""
    value = (os.environ if environ is None else environ).get(
        "FORGE_PR_CHECK_MEMORY_MAX", MEMORY_MAX).strip()
    return None if value.lower() in ("", "off") else value


def scope_prefix(memory_max):
    """What runs a command in its own user scope under memory_max."""
    return ["systemd-run", "--user", "--scope", "--quiet", "--collect",
            "-p", "MemoryMax=" + memory_max, "-p", "MemorySwapMax=0",
            "-p", "OOMPolicy=continue", "--"]


def memory_cap(memory_max, env, run=sh, out=print):
    """The prefix for each step: scope_prefix(memory_max) once a scope
    is seen to start, else none, saying so."""
    if memory_max is None:
        return []
    prefix = scope_prefix(memory_max)
    got = run(prefix + ["true"], env=env, timeout=60)
    if got.returncode != 0:
        why = ((got.stderr or "") + (got.stdout or "")).strip()
        out("UNCAPPED: could not start a user scope (rc=%d%s); the steps "
            "run without a memory limit"
            % (got.returncode, ": " + why.splitlines()[-1] if why else ""))
        return []
    out("  each step limited to %s" % memory_max)
    return prefix


def tail(text, lines=TAIL_LINES):
    return "\n".join(text.rstrip("\n").splitlines()[-lines:])


def check(wt, env, run=sh, steps=None, prefix=()):
    """Every step that applies to the head, each run even if an earlier
    one failed, and none retried, each after `prefix` (memory_cap).
    Returns (ok, results)."""
    results = []
    for name, args, only_if in STEPS if steps is None else steps:
        if only_if and not os.path.exists(os.path.join(wt, only_if)):
            continue
        started = time.monotonic()
        got = run(list(prefix) + args, cwd=wt, env=env,
                  timeout=STEP_TIMEOUT_S)
        results.append({"name": name, "rc": got.returncode,
                        "seconds": int(time.monotonic() - started),
                        "tail": tail((got.stdout or "") + (got.stderr or ""))})
    return all(r["rc"] == 0 for r in results), results


def start_next_tick(popen=None, checkout=None):
    """Start one `forge-pr-check --post` tick through forge-cron-run,
    detached, and return its argv. Not waited for: the caller is about
    to exit. The tick uses the default state directory, as cron's do,
    and the checkout this worker checked from."""
    popen = popen or subprocess.Popen
    argv = [CRON_RUN] + list(NEXT_TICK)
    env = dict(os.environ)
    if checkout:
        env["FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT"] = checkout
    popen(argv, env=env, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=subprocess.DEVNULL,
          stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, start_new_session=True, close_fds=True)
    return argv


def worker(repo, state_dir, sha, pr, run=sh, out=print, clock=now_utc,
           post=None, chain=None, slot=1, memory_max=None):
    """Check sha, pull request pr's head, now, in this process, in
    `slot`, each step limited to memory_max (None: no limit)."""
    os.makedirs(state_dir, exist_ok=True)
    started = clock()
    held = try_lock(lock_path(state_dir, slot),
                    "#%d %s %s" % (pr, sha, iso(started)))
    if held is None:
        out("BUSY: another check holds the worker lock"
            + ("" if slot == 1 else " for slot %d" % slot))
        return 0
    # Whether this head stopped waiting: checked, moved or given up on.
    # Only then is the next tick started, since a chained tick would at
    # once pick a head that is still waiting.
    settled = False
    wt = os.path.join(state_dir, slot_name("wt", slot))
    try:
        status, detail = prepare(repo, wt, sha, pr, run)
        if status == "moved":
            with state_lock(state_dir):
                state = load(state_dir)
                state["waiting"].pop(sha, None)
                save(state_dir, state)
            log(state_dir, "MOVED #%d %s: the head is now %s; not checked"
                % (pr, sha[:10], detail[:10]), started, out)
            settled = True
            return 0
        if status != "ready":
            with state_lock(state_dir):
                state = load(state_dir)
                entry = state["waiting"].get(sha)
                errors = 0
                if entry is not None:
                    errors = entry["errors"] = entry.get("errors", 0) + 1
                save(state_dir, state)
            if errors >= MAX_ERRORS:
                log(state_dir, "GAVE-UP #%d %s after %d failures to prepare "
                    "it; the last: %s" % (pr, sha[:10], errors, detail),
                    started, out)
                if post is not None:
                    post(sha, "error", "not run: could not check the head "
                         "out %d times; the last: %s" % (errors, detail))
                settled = True
            else:
                out("NO-WORKTREE #%d %s: %s" % (pr, sha[:10], detail))
            return 2
        if post is not None:
            post(sha, "pending", "running%s since %s" % (on_host(),
                                                        iso(started)))
        env = step_env(state_dir, slot=slot)
        ok, results = check(wt, env, run,
                            prefix=memory_cap(memory_max, env, run, out))
        for r in results:
            out("  %-20s rc=%-3d %4ds" % (r["name"], r["rc"], r["seconds"]))
            if r["rc"] != 0:
                for line in r["tail"].splitlines():
                    out("    | " + line)
        finished = clock()
        with state_lock(state_dir):
            state = load(state_dir)
            seen = state["waiting"].pop(sha, {}).get("since", iso(started))
            record = {
                "pr": pr, "seen": seen, "started": iso(started),
                "finished": iso(finished), "ok": ok,
                "failed": [r["name"] for r in results if r["rc"] != 0],
                "seconds": sum(r["seconds"] for r in results),
            }
            state["results"][sha] = record
            save(state_dir, state)
        settled = True
        log(state_dir, "VERDICT #%d %s: %s waited=%ds ran=%ds"
            % (pr, sha[:10], verdict_word(record),
               (started - parse(seen)).total_seconds(), record["seconds"]),
            finished, out)
        if post is not None:
            posted = post(sha, *final_status(record))
            with state_lock(state_dir):
                state = load(state_dir)
                if sha in state["results"]:
                    state["results"][sha]["posted"] = posted
                    save(state_dir, state)
        return 0 if ok else 1
    finally:
        held.close()
        # After the lock is free, so the started tick can take it.
        if chain is not None and settled:
            try:
                out("CHAINED %s" % " ".join(chain()[1:]))
            except Exception as err:
                # The verdict is recorded; cron's next tick starts what
                # this could not.
                out("CHAIN-FAILED: %s: %s" % (type(err).__name__, err))


def main(argv=None, run=sh, spawn=spawn_worker, out=print, environ=None):
    environ = os.environ if environ is None else environ
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(
        prog="forge-pr-check", description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    parser.add_argument("--worker", metavar="SHA",
                        help="check SHA now, in this process")
    parser.add_argument("--pr", type=int,
                        help="with --worker: the pull request SHA heads")
    parser.add_argument("--slot", type=int, default=1,
                        help="with --worker: the slot to run in (default 1)")
    parser.add_argument("--post", action="store_true",
                        help="post each verdict as the commit status")
    parser.add_argument("--state-dir", default=None,
                        help="where the queue, the verdicts and the logs "
                        "live (default ~/.local/state/agent-forge/"
                        "<project>/pr-check)")
    parser.add_argument("--merger-dir", default=None,
                        help="with checks.merger_first: the Merger's state "
                        "directory, whose next.json names the pull request "
                        "to check first (default ~/.local/state/agent-forge/"
                        "<project>/merger)")
    parser.add_argument("--checkout", default=environ.get(
        "FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT"), help="the checkout kept at the default "
        "branch (default $FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT)")
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    if args.worker and args.pr is None:
        parser.error("--worker needs --pr")
    if not args.checkout:
        out("NO-REPO: no --checkout, and FORGE_CRON_CHECKOUT is not set")
        return 2
    got = run(["git", "-C", os.path.expanduser(args.checkout), "rev-parse",
               "--show-toplevel"])
    repo = (got.stdout or "").strip()
    if got.returncode != 0 or not repo:
        out("NO-REPO: %s is not a git checkout" % args.checkout)
        return 2
    try:
        project = config.load(os.path.join(repo, config.CONFIG_NAME))
    except config.ConfigError as err:
        out("NO-CONFIG: %s" % err)
        return 2
    configure(project)
    state_dir = args.state_dir or locks.state_dir(project.name, "pr-check",
                                                  environ)
    os.makedirs(state_dir, exist_ok=True)
    post = make_poster(run, out) if args.post else None
    if args.worker:
        chain = (lambda: start_next_tick(checkout=repo)) if args.post else None
        return worker(repo, state_dir, args.worker, args.pr, run, out,
                      post=post, chain=chain, slot=args.slot,
                      memory_max=memory_max_from_env(environ))
    token = mint(run)
    if token is None:
        out("NO-TOKEN: could not mint %s's token" % POSTER)
        return 2
    merger_dir = None
    if MERGER_FIRST:
        merger_dir = args.merger_dir or locks.state_dir(project.name,
                                                        "merger", environ)
    return tick(state_dir, token, run, spawn, out, post=post,
                slots=slots_from_env(environ), checkout=repo,
                merger_dir=merger_dir)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
